<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baltistan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Little Tibet</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baltistan is a high mountain region in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilgit-baltistan">Gilgit-Baltistan</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, around the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> and its tributaries, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skardu">Skardu</a> as its main town. Its people, the Balti, speak a Tibetic language and are mainly Shia and Noorbakhshi Muslims. Ruled by local dynasties such as the Maqpon, it was conquered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dogras">Dogras</a> in 1840, and it contains K2 and the Baltoro Glacier.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baltistan.jpg" alt="Baltistan" width="320" height="317" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: US Central Intelligence Agency · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kashmir_Region_November_2019.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
